    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm looking at a house contract here and it keeps mentioning an \"escrow agent\". i'm a bit confused about what they actually do and why my money has to go to them instead of just the seller. can u explain?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! An escrow agent acts as an unbiased third party to ensure that both the buyer and seller adhere to the contract terms. They hold the buyer's deposit to protect the buyer and the seller's property. When the buyer and seller fulfill their obligations, such as inspections and repairs, the escrow agent facilitates the transfer of the funds at the closing. This helps prevent fraud, encourages trust, and ensures everyone plays by the rules.",
