    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay that makes sense. but it feels a bit weird to just hand over a huge chunk of money to some random person/company and just hope they do the right thing. isn't that risky? like what exactly are they guarding or holding for me while we wait for the closing date?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your concerns. The escrow agent is not random; they are typically certified and must follow strict regulations to protect both parties' interests. The funds held by the escrow company are usually invested in short-term, low-risk securities. The agent is bound by law to act in your best interests and to ensure the funds are safely secured until the closing. They are there to facilitate the rightful exchange of funds and property, serving as a neutral party to make the transaction smooth and secure. You can also request and review all transactions and adjustments regularly during the process for your peace of mind.",
