      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's natural to feel that way, you'd be surprised at how the involvement of an escrow agent actually reduces the potential for impropriety. These agents work for escrow companies that are insurance-backed entities, which means they're obligated to keep your money safe. Moreover, they close only when they know both parties are satisfied with the transaction. If someone were to attempt to improperly tap into the funds, the escrow company could potentially face serious legal consequences, including asset forfeiture and closure of the business. The industry's regulatory framework aims to prevent such issues and offers you protection throughout the transaction process.",
